cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GOAA: Governance-Oriented Agent Architecture (GOAA 2.0)"
abstract: "This repository is the 2.0 open-source engineering implementation of the GOAA governance-oriented agent architecture. It solves the problem of 'how to make AI controllable' rather than 'how to make AI work' - with 100% human decision rights as the mother axiom, files as the carrier of memory and rules, and three-semantic disambiguation (human/machine/programming). A non-engineer, non-CS author designed it: it proves the understanding threshold of governance-oriented architecture belongs to ordinary people."
authors:
  - family-names: "Yin"
    given-names: "Jianlong"
    website: "https://github.com/roebin87"
